      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking an aspirin or extra magnesium might seem like a potential temporary fix, but it's essential to avoid self-diagnosing and treating symptoms without professional guidance, as this could be risky. A pharmaceutical self-treatment doesn't guarantee that the underlying issue will be resolved and there's always the risk of side effects or masking more serious problems. If overtaking pain and a blackout have happened at least once, proceeding to the ER for a thorough evaluation could be warranted to ensure there isn't a serious health concern. It's always better to be safe and address the potentially underlying issue with a professional.",
      "source": "target",
